    "created_at": "2023-05-23T09:11:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-05-23T09:11:18Z",
    "body": "I think (unless I misunderstand the meaning of step 1 https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsing-the-web.html#scroll-to-the-fragment-identifier) that both for step 1 and step 2 it would make sense to say that the sequential navigation starting point should be unset, so that you're effectively bounced back to the start of the document both visually, *and* in terms of focus sequence. This would make the keyboard experience much more controlled and consistent (compared to the current experience, where yes *visually* you're bounced to the top, but a subsequent `Tab` jumps you all the way back to where you originally were).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
