    "body": "> I don't think it should be unset for step 1. Pages might use fragments for client side navigation or storage.\r\n\r\nthen they should also `preventDefault` / cancel the event though to suppress both a visual scrolling behaviour *and* then the resetting of the sequential navigation starting point, no? (i.e. if they're using it in a non-standard way / hooking into it for other JS-based functionality)",
